            <ArticleTitle>Cockroach allergens: function, structure and allergenicity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>960-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cockroach allergy is a widespread health problem in the world, associated with the development of asthma. The German and American cockroach species are important producers of a wide variety of allergens. Knowledge of their structure and function contributes to understand their role in allergy and to design tools for diagnosis and immunotherapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
